# See https://help.github.com/articles/ignoring-files/ for more about ignoring files.

# dependencies
/node_modules
/.pnp
.pnp.*
.yarn/*
!.yarn/patches
!.yarn/plugins
!.yarn/releases
!.yarn/versions

# testing
/coverage

# next.js
/.next/
/out/

# production
/build

# misc
.DS_Store
*.pem

# debug
npm-debug.log*
yarn-debug.log*
yarn-error.log*
.pnpm-debug.log*

# env files (can opt-in for committing if needed)
.env*

# vercel
.vercel

# typescript
*.tsbuildinfo
next-env.d.ts

# generated by scripts/build-data.mjs from ../DataModel
# (committed so Vercel can build without source data)
/app/works/[paintingId]/

# Source material, kept locally and never committed.
# DataModel/ is the record of origin; MS-CS-00N/ holds the scans it points at, one
# directory per physical box, and Video Archive/ the 25 GB of masters. The site is a
# consumer of all of them: the generated bundle in data/ and the copies in
# public/scans/ ARE committed, which is what lets Vercel build without any of this
# (see the guard in build-data.mjs).
/DataModel/
/MS-CS-001/
/MS-CS-002/
/Video Archive/

# NOTE, not a rule: OneDrive syncs this Desktop and leaves conflict copies named
# "<file> 2.<ext>" — stale snapshots, not edits. They compile, so tsc and eslint pass
# them in silence, and they inflate check-export's page count when they land in out/.
# Deliberately NOT ignored: an ignore rule hides them, and hidden is how thirteen of
# them survived. Let them show up untracked, then delete them.
